  "examples": [
    {
      "coptic": "ⲙⲡⲣⲧⲣⲉⲡⲉⲕϩⲏⲧ **ⲣⲓⲕⲉ** ⲉⲛⲉⲥϩⲓⲟⲟⲩⲉ",
      "english": "Let not thine heart turn aside to her ways :",
      "source": "Proverbs 7",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:ot.prov.coptot:7",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲙⲡⲛⲁⲩ ϩⲱⲱϥ ⲉⲧⲉⲣⲉⲡⲉⲕϫⲁϫⲉ ⲛⲁⲕⲁⲥⲕⲥ ⲉϩⲟⲩⲛ ⲉⲣⲟⲕ · ⲉⲧⲉⲡⲁⲓ ⲡⲉ ⲡⲇⲓⲁⲃⲟⲗⲟⲥ ϣⲁⲕ**ⲣⲓⲕⲉ** ⲙⲡⲉⲕⲙⲁⲁϫⲉ ⲉⲣⲟϥ ⲛϥⲡⲉϩⲧⲗⲱⲙⲥ ⲉⲡⲉⲥⲏⲧ ⲉⲣⲟϥ · ⲛⲅⲟⲩⲱⲛ ⲙⲡⲉⲕϩⲏⲧ · ⲛⲅⲱⲙⲅ ⲛⲧⲙⲁⲧⲟⲩ ⲛⲧⲁϥⲁⲡⲟⲃⲁⲗⲉ ⲙⲙⲟⲥ ⲛⲁⲕ ·",
      "english": "At the moment when thine enemy, that is to say, the Devil, whispereth unto thee, thou dost incline thine ear to him, and he poureth into it stinkingness, and thou openest thy heart, and dost swallow the venom which he poureth into thee.",
      "source": "Instructions of Apa Pachomius in MERC.AR in Budge ed. - part 1",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:pachomius.instructions.budge:1-34",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ϩⲟⲙⲟⲓⲱⲥ ⲟⲛ ⲉⲣϣⲁⲛⲡⲥⲱⲧⲙ ϣⲱⲡ ⲉⲣⲟϥ ⲛⲧⲉⲥⲙⲏ ⲉⲧⲛⲟⲧⲙ ⲙⲛⲧⲁⲡⲁⲧⲏ ⲛⲛϫⲱ ⲉⲧⲥⲟⲟϥ ⲉⲧⲙⲙⲁⲩ · ⲛⲧⲉⲡϩⲏⲧ **ⲣⲓⲕⲉ** ⲛⲥⲱⲟⲩ · ϣⲁⲩⲥⲱⲕ ⲙⲙⲟϥ ⲉⲡⲉⲥⲏⲧ ⲉⲡⲉⲩⲧⲁⲕⲟ ·",
      "english": "So also is it in the case of the hearing. If the ear receiveth the pleasant sound (or, voice), and the deceitful words of lewdness which accompany it, then doth the heart incline thereto, and they drag down the heart into destruction.",
      "source": "On Susanna",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:pschrysostom.susanna.budge:1-63",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    }
  ],
